<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">2008 financial crisis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2007">2007</a>–<a href="/years/2008">2008</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 2008 financial crisis was a worldwide financial crisis that began in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> with the subprime mortgage crisis of early 2007, when mortgage-backed securities tied to U.S. real estate collapsed in value. It spread to global institutions and climaxed with the bankruptcy of Lehman Brothers in September 2008 which triggered a stock market crash and bank runs in several countries. Governments answered with bailouts such as the $700 billion Troubled Asset Relief Program and with monetary and fiscal policy. Some 8.7 million American jobs were lost, and the crisis worsened the Great Recession and contributed to crises in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iceland">Iceland</a> and the eurozone.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>2008 financial crisis</b> is said to have shown flaws in Christian democratic welfare.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/christian-democracy">Christian democracy · Critiques &amp; Debates</a></li><li><blockquote>The protests that followed the <b>2008 financial crisis</b>, including Occupy, the Indignados and the Gilets jaunes, have been described as populist, as have parties that grew out of them, such as Podemos and India's Aam Aadmi Party.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/populism">Populism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>…parties rose in some countries, among them Podemos, Syriza, Die Linke and La France Insoumise, and in the 2010s Jeremy Corbyn in the United Kingdom and Bernie Sanders in the United States led left-wing revivals within established parties, amid growing inequality and discontent after the <b>2008 financial crisis</b>.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/socialism">Socialism · Legacy</a></li></ul></section>
